Findings: [minor] CM-01 core/SkinSetup.lua:205-219 (KCM.SkinPanelText): The stock-colour line that stays in SkinPanelText is a plain SetTextColor that the library does not record. Because S.Text is now recorded with the panel flag, any library repaint while the panel is ignored replays S.Text, which calls P.unpaint and puts the template colour back. That happens on a skin switch or on SetIgnore turning the panel switch on. The state colours (the disabled gray, the gray on 'Macro not created yet', the gold on a GameFontHighlight template) then show as white or gold until the Options OnLooksChanged listener re-renders the page. A second way this shows: P.tint saves the colour a string had before its first tint. If the panel goes back to skinned after a row was drawn while ignored, the saved colour is the state colour. If the row's state then changes while skinned, the next unpaint briefly restores the old state colour. Both effects only last until the page re-renders, and the implementer flagged the first. No test covers a skin switch with the panel ignored and no re-render. | [minor] CM-01 Ka0sAddonsCommonTasks docs/2026-10-30-SKIN_LIBRARY_FOLLOWUPS (execution record / RESUME / exceptions): ConsumableMaster departs from the v1.81.0 'What a consumer owes' list on the LK-05 point ('deletes its own give-back (ConsumableMaster's KCM.SkinPanelText)'), and the reason is recorded only in the addon repo's commit message and docs. The bundle has no record that this owed item was kept on purpose, so a later sweep could delete it and break SKIN-7. | [nit] CM-01 tests/test_skin_surfaces.lua:221-238 (buildWidget): The fixture now wraps CreateFrame so that a FontString built from a template gets that template's font object, because the kit's mock_paint recorder does not do this. Without the wrap, the library's font restore has nothing to put back and two tests fail. The fix belongs in the shared kit, not in one addon. Other addons that test S.Text with `{ panel = true }` will hit the same gap. | [nit] CM-02 docs/smoke-tests.md SKIN-7 (unchanged): SKIN-7 keeps its expectations, which is correct, but the mechanism behind it has changed: the library's recorded give-back plus the addon's stock-colour line now produce the result, where the addon's own helper did before. The check does not ask the owner to switch skins while the panel is ignored and a Stat Priority or Buttons page is open, which is the one path the first finding affects.
